{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39649190",
      "title": "Best Practice: Storing Components in Files & Using a Good Project Structure",
      "sourceHash": "f5d98aa514013aea16483e76377d383675e3ab07fd003008c0778692b43a6a6a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.36,
          "end": 2.37,
          "en": "So now that we did learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.37,
          "end": 5.19,
          "en": "about some key React concepts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.19,
          "end": 8.64,
          "en": "most importantly about Components and Props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.64,
          "end": 12.24,
          "en": "before we dive deeper into React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.24,
          "end": 15.96,
          "en": "and have a look at more React concepts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.96,
          "end": 18.39,
          "en": "I wanna restructure this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.39,
          "end": 19.95,
          "en": "because at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.95,
          "end": 23.19,
          "en": "all our Components, the Header component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.19,
          "end": 26.79,
          "en": "the CoreConcept component, and the App component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.79,
          "end": 30.9,
          "en": "all these Components are in the same single file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.9,
          "end": 35.16,
          "en": "They are all in this App.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.16,
          "end": 37.95,
          "en": "And of course, technically this works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.95,
          "end": 42.54,
          "en": "but it's not recommended to have them all in the same file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.54,
          "end": 45.27,
          "en": "because as your React project grows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.27,
          "end": 48.09,
          "en": "and as you add more and more Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.09,
          "end": 50.25,
          "en": "this file would grow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.25,
          "end": 52.26,
          "en": "And working on those Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.26,
          "end": 55.62,
          "en": "and finding the different Components would get harder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.62,
          "end": 59.25,
          "en": "and harder the more Components you have in that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.25,
          "end": 62.52,
          "en": "Therefore, you typically store different Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.52,
          "end": 64.02,
          "en": "in different files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.02,
          "end": 66,
          "en": "And having multiple Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66,
          "end": 69.96000000000001,
          "en": "in the same file is a very rare exception,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.96000000000001,
          "end": 72.63,
          "en": "which you typically only go for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.63,
          "end": 76.56,
          "en": "if two Components are super closely related",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.56,
          "end": 79.47,
          "en": "and really only work with each other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.47,
          "end": 82.62,
          "en": "So if you have a component that really can't be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.62,
          "end": 84.75,
          "en": "anywhere else in the application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.75,
          "end": 87,
          "en": "not even theoretically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87,
          "end": 89.13,
          "en": "So here, of course, every component can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.13,
          "end": 91.8,
          "en": "at least in theory be used standalone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.8,
          "end": 94.86,
          "en": "and therefore here, I'll create new files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.86,
          "end": 98.4,
          "en": "for the CoreConcept and the Header component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.4,
          "end": 100.2,
          "en": "And you typically do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.2,
          "end": 103.13300000000001,
          "en": "in a separate Components subfolder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.13300000000001,
          "end": 106.44,
          "en": "which you add in the SRC folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.44,
          "end": 108.72,
          "en": "Technically, this is not required,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 108.72,
          "end": 112.62,
          "en": "but it's a common choice and very common pattern.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.62,
          "end": 115.32,
          "en": "And then in that Components folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.32,
          "end": 118.59,
          "en": "you would create your component code files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 118.59,
          "end": 123.59,
          "en": "And here the convention is to give those files the same name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.41,
          "end": 126.99,
          "en": "as the component name of the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.99,
          "end": 129.153,
          "en": "that will be stored in that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 129.99,
          "end": 133.23,
          "en": "So if I wanna store that Header component in a file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 133.23,
          "end": 135.96,
          "en": "I would name the file Header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.96,
          "end": 139.02,
          "en": "and then add the .jsx extension",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.02,
          "end": 141.753,
          "en": "since I'll have some JSX code in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.76,
          "end": 147.93,
          "en": "With that, we can then grab this Header component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.93,
          "end": 151.87,
          "en": "from the App.jsx file, and cut it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.85,
          "end": 155.04,
          "en": "and add it in this Header.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.78,
          "end": 159.32999999999998,
          "en": "And since in that component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 159.32999999999998,
          "end": 163.29,
          "en": "I also refer to the ReactDescriptions array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.29,
          "end": 166.44,
          "en": "and this genRandomInt function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.44,
          "end": 169.8,
          "en": "I'll also cut and paste these two things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.8,
          "end": 172.053,
          "en": "to this Header.jsx file like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 174.06,
          "end": 177.45,
          "en": "With that, we outsourced this component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 177.45,
          "end": 180.15,
          "en": "into its own separate file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 180.15,
          "end": 182.16,
          "en": "Now we just have to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 182.16,
          "end": 185.64,
          "en": "that we can still use it in the App.jsx file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 185.64,
          "end": 189.003,
          "en": "because that is still where I do want to use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.87,
          "end": 192.54,
          "en": "And to make this component function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192.54,
          "end": 196.95,
          "en": "usable in another file, we have to export it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 196.95,
          "end": 201,
          "en": "And that can be done in JavaScript with the export keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 201,
          "end": 203.22,
          "en": "And now we can either export it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 203.22,
          "end": 205.35,
          "en": "as a named export like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 205.35,
          "end": 207.72,
          "en": "or as the default export like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 207.72,
          "end": 210.75,
          "en": "by adding the default keyword as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 210.75,
          "end": 212.67000000000002,
          "en": "And in most React projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 212.67000000000002,
          "end": 215.94,
          "en": "it's this default export approach that's being used,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 215.94,
          "end": 219.003,
          "en": "but ultimately, it is up to you, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 219.9,
          "end": 222.69,
          "en": "Now with this export statement added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 222.69,
          "end": 225.487,
          "en": "we then have to go back to the App.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 225.487,
          "end": 227.94,
          "en": "And there we have to add an import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 227.94,
          "end": 230.67000000000002,
          "en": "to use that Header component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 230.67000000000002,
          "end": 233.01,
          "en": "We can then name it Header here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 233.01,
          "end": 234.96,
          "en": "It's important that it does start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 234.96,
          "end": 237.12,
          "en": "with that capital character.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 237.12,
          "end": 241.14,
          "en": "And then we can import from ./components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 241.14,
          "end": 243.33,
          "en": "diving into that Components folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 243.33,
          "end": 247.65,
          "en": "seen relative from that App.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 247.65,
          "end": 251.463,
          "en": "And then they're pointed Header.jsx, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 253.2,
          "end": 254.97,
          "en": "With this import added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 254.97,
          "end": 257.67,
          "en": "this Header component can still be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 257.67,
          "end": 260.25,
          "en": "in the JSX code of the App component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 260.25,
          "end": 265.25,
          "en": "We just also have to cut and paste the React image import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 265.41,
          "end": 269.01,
          "en": "over to the Header.jsx file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 269.01,
          "end": 271.92,
          "en": "because we're using this React image there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 271.92,
          "end": 276.92,
          "en": "in the JSX code of that Header component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 276.96,
          "end": 280.5,
          "en": "Though here, we then also have to adjust the path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 280.5,
          "end": 284.4,
          "en": "because we're now in a file, the Header.jsx file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 284.4,
          "end": 287.90999999999997,
          "en": "which is inside of a nested folder in the source folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 287.90999999999997,
          "end": 291.45,
          "en": "So if we want to target a file that's in the assets folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 291.45,
          "end": 293.90999999999997,
          "en": "this path won't work anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 293.90999999999997,
          "end": 297.57,
          "en": "because we now, first of all, have to go up one level",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 297.57,
          "end": 299.22,
          "en": "out of the Components folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 299.22,
          "end": 302.58,
          "en": "directly into the source folder before we can dive back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 302.58,
          "end": 305.04,
          "en": "into the assets folder and look for the image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 305.04,
          "end": 307.68,
          "en": "And therefore, here in this import path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 307.68,
          "end": 309.51,
          "en": "in the Header.jsx file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 309.51,
          "end": 313.23,
          "en": "we have to go up one level with ../",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 313.23,
          "end": 315.66,
          "en": "and then we're in the source folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 315.66,
          "end": 317.43,
          "en": "and we can dive into the assets folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 317.43,
          "end": 319.53,
          "en": "and then look for the image there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 319.53,
          "end": 323.16,
          "en": "And with this path adjusted and all files saved,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 323.16,
          "end": 326.97,
          "en": "if you go back, you should see the same result as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 326.97,
          "end": 329.19,
          "en": "But now we got the Header component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 329.19,
          "end": 332.25,
          "en": "in its own separate file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 332.25,
          "end": 334.26,
          "en": "And we can and should now do the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 334.26,
          "end": 336.96,
          "en": "for the CoreConcept component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 336.96,
          "end": 339.06,
          "en": "For that in the Components folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 339.06,
          "end": 342.453,
          "en": "we can add the CoreConcept.jsx file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 343.38,
          "end": 347.28,
          "en": "and then grab this CoreConcept function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 347.28,
          "end": 352.28,
          "en": "cut it, and added here in this CoreConcept.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 353.55,
          "end": 355.68,
          "en": "And we don't need to add anything else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 355.68,
          "end": 358.53,
          "en": "except for the export statement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 358.53,
          "end": 361.41,
          "en": "Again, using this default export syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 361.41,
          "end": 365.9,
          "en": "so that in App.jsx, we can then also import CoreConcept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 367.08,
          "end": 371.703,
          "en": "from ./components CoreConcept.jsx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 372.75,
          "end": 376.5,
          "en": "So that this CoreConcept component is still available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 376.5,
          "end": 378.303,
          "en": "in this App.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 379.8,
          "end": 382.17,
          "en": "And with that, if we save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 382.17,
          "end": 383.67,
          "en": "this also still works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 383.67,
          "end": 386.88,
          "en": "but now every component is in its own file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 386.88,
          "end": 390.093,
          "en": "and therefore, we are using a common best practice.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}